  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \nA short wave will move through shallow west northwest flow this\nweekend which will bring increasing high and mid clouds, particularly\ntonight into Sunday. Then, an expansive mid level ridge will\ntranslate east, becoming centered over the Tennessee Valley Tuesday\ninto Wednesday. \n\nIt is not out of the question that there could be a few sprinkles out\nof the mid deck tomorrow, but the chance of measurable rain is\nextremely low. So, dry conditions will continue into mid week.\n\nThere remains the potential for a front to sag into the area later in\nthe week as the mid level high gets suppressed south while a short \nwave moves across the Great Lakes. But timing and occurrence are \nuncertain.\n\nA warming trend will occur with temperatures getting into the lower\n90s next week, possibly even some mid 90s. Dew points will rise once\nlow level southerly flow become established. Heat indices could\napproach 100 by Wednesday.",
